## Notes on acceptance criteria

This component satisfies the requested subset:

### Bucket
- versioning enabled
- SSE enabled with `AES256`
- public access blocked

### RDS
- deletion protection enabled
- backup retention = 7 days
- not publicly accessible
- prod uses `multiAz: true`
- encryption enabled

### Secret
- DB password comes from `config.requireSecret(...)`
- generated connection string is wrapped in `pulumi.secret(...)`

### IAM
- OIDC trust for Kubernetes service account
- least-privilege bucket access
- no wildcard actions in prod policy

---

## Install dependencies

```bash
npm install @pulumi/pulumi @pulumi/aws
```

---

## Example usage

```bash
pulumi stack init dev
pulumi config set aws:region us-east-1
pulumi config set canonical-app:vpcId vpc-xxxxxxxx
pulumi config set --path canonical-app:privateSubnetIds[0] subnet-aaaaaaa
pulumi config set --path canonical-app:privateSubnetIds[1] subnet-bbbbbbb
pulumi config set canonical-app:dbSecurityGroupId sg-xxxxxxxx
pulumi config set canonical-app:oidcProviderArn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLE
pulumi config set canonical-app:oidcProviderUrl https://oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLE
pulumi config set canonical-app:k8sNamespace app
pulumi config set canonical-app:k8sServiceAccountName web
pulumi config set canonical-app:dbUsername appuser
pulumi config set canonical-app:dbName appdb
pulumi config set --secret canonical-app:dbPassword 'supersecret'
pulumi up
```

